WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.350
A dog. A cake.

2
00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:06.020
«Le chien mange le gâteau.»
The dog eats the cake.

3
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:08.730
Now flip it, so the cake comes first:

4
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.240
the cake is eaten by the dog.

5
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.210
How do you build that in French?

6
00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:14.340
Here's the twist.

7
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.410
French uses that pattern
less than English does.

8
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:19.550
So when French speakers don't want it,

9
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.310
what do they say instead?

10
00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:25.300
In this mission, you'll watch
the dog and the cake swap seats.

11
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:29.350
Then you'll sort look-alike sentences
with a two-question flowchart.

12
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.710
Your mission: crack how
French says what's done,

13
00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:36.050
and by whom, and spot when
it takes another route.
